+// True when the UI process that launched this process sent an SDK aligned behavior bitmap narrower
+// than this build's own, which is the only run-time evidence available here that it runs an older
+// WebKit and therefore numbers its IPC messages by a different enumeration. Recorded once per
+// process by XPCServiceEntryPoint.mm, read once by AuxiliaryProcess::initialize.
+//
+// The width test separates 16.0 through 16.3, which send two words, from 16.4 onwards, which send
+// three. It does not separate generations inside either group: a 16.4 or 17.x peer reads as
+// same-generation and is not translated, while a 16.0, 16.2 or 16.3 peer reads as older and gets
+// translated with 16.1 tables that do not match its numbering. Both are blind spots of the signal,
+// not of this call. The pairings this project ships, a 16.1 UI process with this build and this
+// build with another copy of itself, sit on opposite sides of the width and are settled by it.
+bool peerIsOlderGeneration();
+
 } // namespace WebKit
 
